<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 578 bln lire of Italy 3-yr BTP.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 578 bln lire of Italy 3-yr BTP.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 578 billion lire of three-year fixed-rate bonds (BTP) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 200 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 5.543 trillion lire at the open auction for the February 15, 2000 paper, against 2.5 trillion lire worth of bonds on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 98.55 from 98.60 and gross yield at 6.67 percent against 6.64 percent at the previous sale on April 16.</p>
</text>
